      "weather": "Overcast",
      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PAPER SHREDDER (1) was out of character last run when missing the frame, finishing sixth (22.98) in a Free For All at this track. Generally fast to begin but always back from the wide draw last time. Form here at the trip sound including nine wins. Safe beginner who draws ideally on the inside. Should be very hard to beat this time. TOMMY TSUNAMI (8) stuck on well last time to finish 0.8 lengths back in third (23.11) at this track in a Grade 4 over 400m. Expected to be in this for a long way. MY MOON SHADOW (2) pinged the lids and was in the firing line early but drifted out of it when 5th at Maitland in Grade 4/5 company. Solid record here at the distance winning six races. Smart beginner who should take advantage of the low draw. Key player if finds best. FASCINATE GLORY (6) is in winning form and worth including in the main hopes.",
